  "graph": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "1",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "Study: a linear multitrack recorder, rebuilt with Phase 4's tools.\n\nFive tracks (drums, bass, chords, lead, and a vocal you record), each a Track block (fader, pan, mute, solo) with a reverb send and a stem file; a reverb bus and a delay bus; a master with a compressor, a limiter, and meters. The clips are placed in the song (`start` At beat): chords from bar 5 to bar 13, lead from bar 9, so playing from any bar finds each one where it belongs. Automation on the lead's volume, a punch range for the vocal on bars 5 and 6, and markers for the sections, all on the ruler. The Mixer panel is the mixer window: each Track block pinned as a channel strip with its send under it, the bus returns, the master fader with its meter, and the recording controls, each section under a label.\n\nClick the ruler at bar 9 and press Space: everything plays from there. The click is the metronome button, live only, so it's never in the export.\n\nThe Song panel is the song in time, a lane per placed clip and the automation: drag a block to move it, its end to trim it.\n\nWhat a recorder does that this can't: comp takes, or fade a clip. Read docs/GAPS.md for the full list."
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            0.0,
            -560.0
          ],
          "size": [
            760.0,
            230.0
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "3",
        "kind": "clip",
        "config": {
          "file": "../examples/assets/drums.wav",
          "channels": 1
        },
        "params": {
          "at": 0.0,
          "loop": true,
          "start": "at"
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            600.0,
            0.0
          ],
          "label": "Drums"
        }
      },
